(594668, 60459, 259, '<td valign="top">i wouldn''t crop the foreground out.  it helps so much to give a sence of depth.  the inclusion of a foreground was one of the reasons i gave it a 10.</td>', 'i wouldn''t crop the foreground out.  it helps so much to give a sence of depth.  the inclusion of a foreground was one of the reasons i gave it a 10.', '2004-02-23 13:52:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(594731, 60221, 11693, '<td valign="top">I too like the b&amp;w choice.  Symmetry is an issue for me in this shot.  As was stated before, there is too much area to the right of the boat.  It is not quite in the center of the rule of thirds area.  The boat itself is caught at a bad angle as it too does not look symmetrical.  The transom appears to have two differnt angles on the left and on the right.  It looks like a boat that I might try to draw and not get quite right.  Perhaps a shot more from the side instead of from the stern might be better.  It just gives the photo an off balance look to me.  I like the texture of the exposed shore but the extra white is distracting to me as well.  Good luck and I hope that this does not sound too harsh.  The shot is always there, it is most difficult for me to capture the perfect or best angle, light composition, location, ........  <br/> <br/>David P</td>', 'I too like the b&w choice.  Symmetry is an issue for me in this shot.  As was stated before, there is too much area to the right of the boat.  It is not quite in the center of the rule of thirds area.  The boat itself is caught at a bad angle as it too does not look symmetrical.  The transom appears to have two differnt angles on the left and on the right.  It looks like a boat that I might try to draw and not get quite right.  Perhaps a shot more from the side instead of from the stern might be better.  It just gives the photo an off balance look to me.  I like the texture of the exposed shore but the extra white is distracting to me as well.  Good luck and I hope that this does not sound too harsh.  The shot is always there, it is most difficult for me to capture the perfect or best angle, light composition, location, ........   David P', '2004-02-23 14:57:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(594767, 59876, 12712, '<td valign="top">I love this picture, one of the best I''ve seen here.</td>', 'I love this picture, one of the best I''ve seen here.', '2004-02-23 15:33:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(594943, 60644, 15506, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the encouragement.  I was very surprised this photo did this well.  I know it was not ''Technically'' correct, but this one kept cathing my eye when I was trying to decide which one to post for the challenge.  I had others that were better focused and brigher, but this one seemed to jump out at me.  So I entered it.  <br/> <br/>9 10''s is quite a surprise.  But it means others also saw whatever it was that I saw in this picture and voted that way.  (Still not sure why I liked this one)<br/></td>', 'Thanks for all the encouragement.  I was very surprised this photo did this well.  I know it was not ''Technically'' correct, but this one kept cathing my eye when I was trying to decide which one to post for the challenge.  I had others that were better focused and brigher, but this one seemed to jump out at me.  So I entered it.   9 10''s is quite a surprise.  But it means others also saw whatever it was that I saw in this picture and voted that way.  (Still not sure why I liked this one)', '2004-02-23 18:10:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(594951, 60045, 17387, '<td valign="top">I believe the line made the difference between ribbon or not.   Whether or not the difference seemed subtle..  I think people really go for the cleaner than clean background most the time.</td>', 'I believe the line made the difference between ribbon or not.   Whether or not the difference seemed subtle..  I think people really go for the cleaner than clean background most the time.', '2004-02-23 18:18:01.000000', NULL, 0),
