(595215, 60020, 6405, '<td valign="top">Very nice shot and it is done with high shutter lag camera which is big plus!!<br/>You are getting better and better every day ! :-)</td>', 'Very nice shot and it is done with high shutter lag camera which is big plus!!You are getting better and better every day ! :-)', '2004-02-23 20:58:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(595257, 60290, 16230, '<td valign="top">[Critique Club] <br/> <br/>Composition: Good, if the subject of the photo is the large building. However, because of the challenge criteria, the water should have been the focal point of the image. Since the water is viewed at such an oblique angle the viewers gaze passes right over it. The other features surrounding the water also tend to lead the eye away from the water. <br/> <br/>Technical Quality: Well done, although the focus seems a bit soft. The use of sepia works well with this image.<br/> <br/>Meeting the Challenge: Room for improvement.  The water should have been emphasized much moreperhaps by shooting from a different angle.<br/> <br/>Creativity: Room for improvement here as well. Maybe a closer shot of the water, possibly from a different angle, would have worked better.<br/> <br/>Overall: A very nice image, but it fails to rise to the challenge.<br/> <br/>I hope this helps. Good luck.<br/> <br/>Regards,<br/>Mick</td>', '[Critique Club]  Composition: Good, if the subject of the photo is the large building. However, because of the challenge criteria, the water should have been the focal point of the image. Since the water is viewed at such an oblique angle the viewers gaze passes right over it. The other features surrounding the water also tend to lead the eye away from the water.  Technical Quality: Well done, although the focus seems a bit soft. The use of sepia works well with this image. Meeting the Challenge: Room for improvement.  The water should have been emphasized much moreperhaps by shooting from a different angle. Creativity: Room for improvement here as well. Maybe a closer shot of the water, possibly from a different angle, would have worked better. Overall: A very nice image, but it fails to rise to the challenge. I hope this helps. Good luck. Regards,Mick', '2004-02-23 21:22:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(595509, 60045, 14620, '<td valign="top">A Birthday cake candle.... now why couldn''t I think of that.  Here I was racking my brain trying to figure out what I could use that wouldn''t really be seen. Hmmmm... Oh well, your shot is absolutely fantastic and is exactly the look I wanted but couldn''t achieve.  Excellent job Aleks!</td>', 'A Birthday cake candle.... now why couldn''t I think of that.  Here I was racking my brain trying to figure out what I could use that wouldn''t really be seen. Hmmmm... Oh well, your shot is absolutely fantastic and is exactly the look I wanted but couldn''t achieve.  Excellent job Aleks!', '2004-02-24 00:36:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(595548, 59876, 11078, '<td valign="top">congrats on this, it almost looks unreal<br/>Well done to achieve such a beautiful picture</td>', 'congrats on this, it almost looks unrealWell done to achieve such a beautiful picture', '2004-02-24 01:25:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(595549, 60505, 11078, '<td valign="top">I couldnt vote on this challenge as my computer crashed from a lightening storm<br/>But congratulations on a well deserved ribbon <br/>I love your image</td>', 'I couldnt vote on this challenge as my computer crashed from a lightening stormBut congratulations on a well deserved ribbon I love your image', '2004-02-24 01:28:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(595617, 60489, 16004, '<td valign="top">*sigh*<br/> <br/>yes, i know, I have a wonky head.  The bizarre thing is, I actually rotated it ACW before submission...  And the horizon is (give or take half a degree) at right angles with the sides.  But, yes, it looks like a ski slope.  must be an optical illusion with the foreground or something.  tsck.  nevermind, it didn''t do so badly (for what I felt was a more than a tad boring shot anyway)</td>', '*sigh* yes, i know, I have a wonky head.  The bizarre thing is, I actually rotated it ACW before submission...  And the horizon is (give or take half a degree) at right angles with the sides.  But, yes, it looks like a ski slope.  must be an optical illusion with the foreground or something.  tsck.  nevermind, it didn''t do so badly (for what I felt was a more than a tad boring shot anyway)', '2004-02-24 04:04:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(595781, 60491, 806, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by dsidwell:</b></div><hr/><i>I''m not sure why (but someday I''ll figure it out), but this photo had considerable grain in it that was difficult to remove.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Just curious if this has anything to do with the 1/320 shutter speed. f8 seems to have been large enough to let in light, I am wondering if 320 is too much. - Just a thought from someone who really doesn''t know for sure. :)</td>', 'Originally posted by dsidwell:I''m not sure why (but someday I''ll figure it out), but this photo had considerable grain in it that was difficult to remove.  Just curious if this has anything to do with the 1/320 shutter speed. f8 seems to have been large enough to let in light, I am wondering if 320 is too much. - Just a thought from someone who really doesn''t know for sure. :)', '2004-02-24 08:44:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(595836, 60143, 1779, '<td valign="top">great shot. should''ve been at least in the top 10. love the colors and the sky and of course the perfect focus in the wood stick in the center while everything else is moving. ribbon worthy, LM</td>', 'great shot. should''ve been at least in the top 10. love the colors and the sky and of course the perfect focus in the wood stick in the center while everything else is moving. ribbon worthy, LM', '2004-02-24 09:48:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(596534, 60143, 8699, '<td valign="top">Looks great! Love the color but agree with the placement. It''s just missing a little something that, if you had it, would have put it over the top. Maybe you cropped a little too much and should have left more of the pinwheel in the photo. Try again for kicks. I''d like to see what you come up with.</td>', 'Looks great! Love the color but agree with the placement. It''s just missing a little something that, if you had it, would have put it over the top. Maybe you cropped a little too much and should have left more of the pinwheel in the photo. Try again for kicks. I''d like to see what you come up with.', '2004-02-24 17:45:22.000000', NULL, 0),
