(602708, 60175, 7778, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments, everyone. <br/> <br/>As most of you recognized, yes, of course, I employed a tripod and slow shutter speed (f 8.0 : 1/30) to render what is here. <br/>A speed slower than this would have tranquilized the beast to a point of false pleasantry, uncharacteristic of the given. To provide an idea of the sheer size and volume of the falls, the image represents approximately one third of the total cascade.</td>', 'Thanks for all the comments, everyone.  As most of you recognized, yes, of course, I employed a tripod and slow shutter speed (f 8.0 : 1/30) to render what is here. A speed slower than this would have tranquilized the beast to a point of false pleasantry, uncharacteristic of the given. To provide an idea of the sheer size and volume of the falls, the image represents approximately one third of the total cascade.', '2004-02-28 14:19:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(602875, 60126, 16672, '<td valign="top">Why did you do that? The fire doesn''t do anything for the over all image it actually looks fake?  I guess you drank to much of that lighter fluid yourself oh well.</td>', 'Why did you do that? The fire doesn''t do anything for the over all image it actually looks fake?  I guess you drank to much of that lighter fluid yourself oh well.', '2004-02-28 16:36:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(603007, 60267, 13390, '<td valign="top"><b>*Greetings from the Critique Club*</b> <br/> <br/>Very interesting shot!  :)<br/> <br/><b>First Impressions:</b> <br/>Honestly, when I first saw this I though "Oh no, not another waterdropshot." But after looking at it for another second I realized how clean it was. Colors seem kinda flat. Overall impression though was that this is a nice shot.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Honestly, I really enjoy the composition here a lot with the off-center subject, it gives it a little bit more of a dynamic feel to it. At first I wasn''t quite sure about the no drop thing, but then I really looked at the shot and thought how hard it must have been to get it that way. Also, not having the drop there kind of steers it away from the cliche. I would second one of the comments mentioned earlier, that there should possibly be a little more action, like having more droplets. Overall, it is a technically sound composition and set-up, very nicely done.<br/> <br/><b>Other:</b> <br/>I do feel there could be a little bit more saturation (even though your blues are quite beautiful), i think it would make it feel more dramatic, but that''s just me, because for some reason it does kinda feel <i>slightly</i> washed out. Excellent focus by the way, very crisp and defined. Also the lighting is quite good. I LOVE the textures of the ripples! The are smooth, flowing, and crisp. I think upping the saturation and contrast would help this a lot.<br/> <br/>Anyways, this is a very cool shot that kind of steers away from the other cliched drops. Very nicely done!<br/> <br/>~Matthew Dykman (goinskiing)<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM if you have any questions, concerns, or comments.</td>', '*Greetings from the Critique Club*  Very interesting shot!  :) First Impressions: Honestly, when I first saw this I though "Oh no, not another waterdropshot." But after looking at it for another second I realized how clean it was. Colors seem kinda flat. Overall impression though was that this is a nice shot. Composition: Honestly, I really enjoy the composition here a lot with the off-center subject, it gives it a little bit more of a dynamic feel to it. At first I wasn''t quite sure about the no drop thing, but then I really looked at the shot and thought how hard it must have been to get it that way. Also, not having the drop there kind of steers it away from the cliche. I would second one of the comments mentioned earlier, that there should possibly be a little more action, like having more droplets. Overall, it is a technically sound composition and set-up, very nicely done. Other: I do feel there could be a little bit more saturation (even though your blues are quite beautiful), i think it would make it feel more dramatic, but that''s just me, because for some reason it does kinda feel slightly washed out. Excellent focus by the way, very crisp and defined. Also the lighting is quite good. I LOVE the textures of the ripples! The are smooth, flowing, and crisp. I think upping the saturation and contrast would help this a lot. Anyways, this is a very cool shot that kind of steers away from the other cliched drops. Very nicely done! ~Matthew Dykman (goinskiing) Feel free to PM if you have any questions, concerns, or comments.', '2004-02-28 19:56:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(603151, 60143, 13390, '<td valign="top"><b>*Greetings from the Critique Club*</b> <br/> <br/>Wow, I feel EXTREMELY unworthy to critique this shot.<br/> <br/><b>First Impressions:</b> <br/> <br/>WOW!! This was my personal favorite in the challenge. The reason is that I believe that the wind element was probably the hardest one to capture and look well. Let''s just say you went well beyond the call of duty their.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/> <br/>Okay, there is only 1, just 1 thing I would do to maybe make this shot better than in already is, and that would be to include more of the pinwheel. But in all reality, that is such a minor technicality in this beautiful shot. I LOVE the blurring of the pinwheel, gives the sense of wind motion, and that fits the challenge extremely well. Personally, I love the center of the pinwheel and how it''s in focus in contrast to the spinning wheels. The clouds also add a lot to this shot by adding more emphasis on wind. plus the white helps the balance a lot. The colors are phenomenal and I like how the colors works with the sky, it just works so well. The lighting is absolutely perfect, it really makes that wood stand out. <br/> <br/><b>Other:</b> <br/>I can''t get over how well this shot was captured, picture perfect. If I had it my way, this shot would have ribboned. This is definetely a shot you should feel proud of. Good luck and I look forward to seeing some of your future work!<br/> <br/>~Matthew Dykman (goinskiing)<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me if you have any questions, comments, or concerns. Thank you.</td>', '*Greetings from the Critique Club*  Wow, I feel EXTREMELY unworthy to critique this shot. First Impressions:  WOW!! This was my personal favorite in the challenge. The reason is that I believe that the wind element was probably the hardest one to capture and look well. Let''s just say you went well beyond the call of duty their. Composition:  Okay, there is only 1, just 1 thing I would do to maybe make this shot better than in already is, and that would be to include more of the pinwheel. But in all reality, that is such a minor technicality in this beautiful shot. I LOVE the blurring of the pinwheel, gives the sense of wind motion, and that fits the challenge extremely well. Personally, I love the center of the pinwheel and how it''s in focus in contrast to the spinning wheels. The clouds also add a lot to this shot by adding more emphasis on wind. plus the white helps the balance a lot. The colors are phenomenal and I like how the colors works with the sky, it just works so well. The lighting is absolutely perfect, it really makes that wood stand out.  Other: I can''t get over how well this shot was captured, picture perfect. If I had it my way, this shot would have ribboned. This is definetely a shot you should feel proud of. Good luck and I look forward to seeing some of your future work! ~Matthew Dykman (goinskiing) Feel free to PM me if you have any questions, comments, or concerns. Thank you.', '2004-02-28 23:49:09.000000', NULL, 0),
